XY is an extremely fast, interactive, customizable Python charting
library for the web, notebooks, and static exports.

Charts are composed declaratively or through matplotlib conventions.
You can fully customize them with Python, CSS, or Tailwind.

With small charts, every point is sent to the browser. For large
charts, the Rust core computes only what the screen needs to display,
based on its resolution. Pan, zoom, hover, and selection can show
full details by running the same process for the new range, and a
selection returns the original rows.
